{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1412170-what-ability-covers-bakeing-aberrant-1st-edition","id":1412170,"title":"What Ability covers bakeing? (Aberrant 1st Edition)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-05T15:16:54-07:00","id":1412170,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon6.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> What Ability covers bakeing? (Aberrant 1st Edition)","content":"Arts &amp; Perform do not seem like a good fit. Is there something I'm missing?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T17:15:31-07:00","id":1412188,"title":"","content":"You might consider Etiquette, Arts, or Survival depending on your whim and/or circumstances. The alternative is to make Cooking a new Ability like Riding or Heavy Weapons. If you go the new ability route I'd make it an Intelligence skill. See the Player's Guide for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","name":"andrewm9","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T18:26:14-07:00","id":1412194,"title":"","content":"I would default to Etiquette.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T19:08:23-07:00","id":1412201,"title":"","content":"Science.<br /> <br /> No, really. Science (including chemistry) genuinely seems like the closest, out of all the existing Abilities, to cooking. And it probably should be under Intelligence anyway.<br /> <br /> There really should be a Crafts ability or something, but I am <i>extremely</i> reluctant to suggest expanding the list of Abilities.<br /> <br /> I guess I could see an argument for Arts, but cooking doesn't seem like a Wits thing so much as Intelligence.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T20:06:48-07:00","id":1412207,"title":"","content":"You don\u2019t always have to use the attribute listed above the ability everytime.Also the Player\u2019s guide already expanded the abilities with things like I listed above, though I would say its probably not worth investing xp in for just cooking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","name":"andrewm9","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T06:21:06-07:00","id":1412265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1412170-what-ability-covers-bakeing-aberrant-1st-edition?p=1412201#post1412201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Science.<br /> <br /> No, really. Science (including chemistry) genuinely seems like the closest, out of all the existing Abilities, to cooking. And it probably should be under Intelligence anyway.<br /> <br /> There really should be a Crafts ability or something, but I am <i>extremely</i> reluctant to suggest expanding the list of Abilities.<br /> <br /> I guess I could see an argument for Arts, but cooking doesn't seem like a Wits thing so much as Intelligence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but cooking is more intuitive. That\u2019s why I said Etiquette. It\u2019s not a perfect fit but it\u2019s the closest one I can think of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T18:35:49-07:00","id":1412366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andrewm9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1412170-what-ability-covers-bakeing-aberrant-1st-edition?p=1412188#post1412188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might consider Etiquette, Arts, or Survival depending on your whim and/or circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Excellent suggestions.<br /> <br /> I think Etiquette &amp; Survival would both work. I do like how some of the Abilities can be used to do the same thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Science.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad your saying that because I was seriously considering Engineering.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andrewm9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1412170-what-ability-covers-bakeing-aberrant-1st-edition?p=1412188#post1412188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The alternative is to make Cooking a new Ability like Riding or Heavy Weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I forgot, do you have to pay full price for alternative Abilities, or are they cheeper, like in Vampire TM Revised?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4428,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","user":"Daredevil","date":". 09-08-2020, 08:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T06:03:48-07:00","id":1412419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1412170-what-ability-covers-bakeing-aberrant-1st-edition?p=1412366#post1412366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I forgot, do you have to pay full price for alternative Abilities, or are they cheeper, like in Vampire TM Revised?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the rules don't give you an xp break for them, but for something as limited as Cooking (compared to say Pilot or Arts) I'd probably make them cheaper. Then again there are original skills like Might that don't seem to have a lot of utility outside of lifting and breaking and even that is made useless (or functionally so) by a single level of Mega Strength (which gives 5 auto successes to the strength + might roll). YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","name":"andrewm9","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}